From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] WSC: refresh registrar crypto for every M1 transaction

The agent's bounded M1 retry cannot recover when the controller's registrar
DH key is unusable.  The controller currently creates a keypair once when the
radio object starts and reuses it for every duplicate M1.  In the observed
failure, all four 5 GHz M2 responses arrived, but each failed at
EVP_PKEY_derive_set_peer because every response carried the same rejected
registrar public key.  The radio remained in wsc_m2_pending and its BSS rows
were never published.

A WSC M1 starts a new protocol transaction.  Reinitialize the controller's
registrar nonce/keypair immediately before parsing each M1; parsing then
replaces the enrollee half with the values from that M1 while retaining the
fresh registrar half for M2.  A duplicate M1 therefore receives an independent
M2 and can recover instead of deterministically repeating the failed key.

Also propagate initial crypto-generation failure from em_t::init rather than
starting a radio object with zero or partial key material.
---
 src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp | 8 ++++++++
 src/em/em.cpp                       | 5 ++++-
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp b/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp
--- a/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp
+++ b/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp
@@ -5581,6 +5581,15 @@ int em_configuration_t::handle_autoconfig_wsc_m1(unsigned char *buff, unsigned
         //return -1;
     }
 
+    // M1 begins a fresh WSC transaction.  Generate a new registrar nonce and
+    // DH keypair before handle_wsc_m1() replaces the enrollee half with the
+    // values carried by this M1.  In particular, a duplicate M1 must not cause
+    // the controller to resend an M2 with the same unusable registrar key.
+    if (m_crypto.init() != 0) {
+        em_printfout("Failed to initialize registrar crypto for WSC M1");
+        return -1;
+    }
+
     tlv = reinterpret_cast<em_tlv_t *>(buff + sizeof(em_raw_hdr_t) + sizeof(em_cmdu_t)); 
     tlv_len = len - static_cast<unsigned int> (sizeof(em_raw_hdr_t) + sizeof(em_cmdu_t));
     em_cmdu_t *cmdu = reinterpret_cast<em_cmdu_t *> (buff + sizeof(em_raw_hdr_t));
diff --git a/src/em/em.cpp b/src/em/em.cpp
--- a/src/em/em.cpp
+++ b/src/em/em.cpp
@@ -2810,7 +2810,10 @@ int em_t::init()
     m_iq.timeout = EM_PROTO_TOUT;
 
     // initialize the crypto
-    m_crypto.init();
+    if (m_crypto.init() != 0) {
+        em_printfout("Failed to initialize WSC crypto");
+        return -1;
+    }
 
     size_t stack_size = 0x800000; /* 8MB */
     pthread_attr_t attr;
